    "bio": "a Representative from Maryland; born Beverly Barton Butcher in Baltimore, Md., July 27, 1932; graduated from National Cathedral School for Girls, Washington, D.C., 1950; attended Hood College, Frederick, Md., 1961-1962; treasurer, Maryland Young Democrats, 1962 and 1965; elected as a Democrat to the Ninety-sixth and to the six succeeding Congresses (January 3, 1979-January 3, 1993); unsuccessful candidate for renomination to the One Hundred Third Congress in 1992; appointed to the Base Closure and Realignment Commission, 1993; died on February 9, 2025, in Frederick, Md.",
